     "text": "#### Arise\nWhen a creature is reduced to 0 hit points and no more than 24 hours has passed since, the Grimm User can approach the corpse to respectfully request the creature’s service in its cause. This act of reverence requires the spirit’s consent, rather than force.\n___\nAs an **Action**, the Grimm User speaks the word \"**Arise**\" and makes a Persuasion (Charisma) Check against a DC equal to the **creature’s CR + 10,** as long as the CR does not exceed the Max Servant CR (equal to the Grimm User’s level + proficiency bonus). The Grimm User can increase the Max Servant CR by expending Grimm Slots when using this ability, increasing the Max CR by 1 per slot used, up to a maximum of 3.\n___\nOn a failure, the Grimm User may expend Grimm Slots to gain additional attempts (one per slot used). If these extra attempts also fail, or if the Grimm User chooses not to use more slots, the soul departs and cannot be recruited by any means.\n___\nOn a success, the recruited creature occupies a servant slot. If no slots are available, the Grimm User must either release an existing servant or forego recruiting the current spirit.\n___\n> Unfinished Business:\n> Because this ability relies on respect for the deceased, the Grimm User may gain a bonus to the Persuasion check by addressing the spirit with sincere words, recognizing its past achievements or speaking to its values and loyalties in life. This roleplay bonus is awarded at the DM’s discretion based on how the Grimm User invokes the spirit’s past deeds or appeals to its desire for purpose, rest, or legacy.\n\n#### Servants\nAs an **Action** the Grimm User uses a Grimm Slot to gain the power of Gate of Caelum and invoke one of its Servants as per the *\"animate dead\"* Spell with the following features:\n\n###### True Animate Dead\nAny trait that affects the \"animate dead\" spell also affects a Servant, however it has the following modifications:\n- Casting time is reduced to an `Action`.\n\t\n- Range increments to Grimm User Prof Bonus x 5 feet.\n\t\n- The size and creature type limitation is removed. \n\t\n- You don't require a `Bonus action` to command a Servant, instead they have their own turn **after** the Grimm User's in the initiative.\n\t\n- The Grimm User may use its `Action` to command a Servant to grant them a Quick Action\n\t\n- If the Grimm User falls unconscious while a Servant is summoned, the DM takes control of the Servant who will do its best to protect and serve its master. \n\t\n- After the 24 hours pass by, the Servant disappears returning to Limbo until its master calls it again.\n\t\n- Servants resonate with the bonds of the Grimm User’s party — when one is gone, the Servant draws upon that void, for each **missing player character** from the party, the Servant's **maximum hit points increase by an amount equal 10 x the Grimm User's Proficiency Level.**\n\n###### Shadow Ghost\nThe Servant takes a spiritual form resembling what would be defined as a shadow ghost gaining the incorporeal movement feature. While in this form the servants have access to a limited form of sentience that embodies their personality during their life and may even be able to recall parts of it.\n\n###### Multiple Servants\nGate of Caelum can summon a max total of servants equivalent to half the Prof Bonus of the Grimm User (Rounded Up).\n\n###### Undying Attunement\nThe Servant is able to attune to a maximum of two magical items, however once a servant is attuned to the item, it will no longer be able to be retrieved. After a Long Rest you are able to choose a magical item which a servant it attuned to and remove it, which will make it lost forever.\n\n> Incorporeal Movement.\n> The Shadow can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\n####  Harvest\nIn order to upgrade an Servant's Soul, the Grimm User can utilize a substance known as **Souls Shards**. When approaching a recently fallen creature, instead of making it join your ranks you can harvest the soul's remain. As an **`Action`** the Grimm User utilizes a Grimm Slot to Soul Harvest up to a number of Creatures equivalent to its Prof Bonus.\n___\nFor all creatures make a **single Harvest (Int) ability check**. Each creature has its own DC, which if succeed it will yield a certain number of Soul Shards that you absorb.\n___\nThe Soul Shards can be used during a Long Rest to upgrade an Adventurer's Soul. \n___\nThe upgrade requirement can be found on Soul Shards Table (Note that an Adventurer's Soul cannot be upgraded beyond the Max Servant CR).\n\n___\n>Upgrading Non Adventurer Soul\n> There are creatures that are not adventurers yet they also have the capacity to grow with the consumption of Soul Shards. This creatures are denoted by terms such as \"young\", \"adult\", \"elder\" or other terms such as \"lesser\" or \"greater\". Consult with the DM which creatures have this capabilities and how much Soul Shards would it take to upgrade it.\n\n____"
