     "name": "Soul Chimera",
     "stage": "awakened",
     "kind": "super",
     "tag": "Super Skill",
     "cost": 2,
     "action": "Action",
     "text": "Ouroboros Vigil empowers the Grimm User to channel the essence within Soul Stones, allowing them to use their full power. By transmuting ambient essence, the Grimm User combines the traits of multiple captured souls, creating a Soul Chimera that embodies unique abilities from these souls.\n___\nAs an **`Action`**, the Grimm User expends 2 Grimm Slots to use the full power of the Soul Stones, by creating a Soul Chimera. The Soul Chimera envelops the Grimm User as the spectral energy surrounds him granting him an additional pool of Hit points and the Abilities, Traits and Stats of when it was first replicated into the stone yet it keeps the his own set of ability scores if higher.\n___\nAs part of the same `Action` the Grimm User can choose to expend and additional Grimm Slot to Channel an additional Soul Stone. While doing the Grimm User must succeed a Intelligence Check against a DC equal to 10 + the average of the CR of the original creatures embodied in the used Soul Stones.\n___\nIf succeed the Soul Chimera also gains the traits and abilities from that creature and in the case of hit points and traits such as ability scores, ac, speed,  the Grimm User can choose to pick whichever is higher and set it as its own.  \n\nIf failed the Soul Chimera is still created with only the features of the first creature however it must roll a d20 for a unexpected effect. There is no limit the number of Soul Stones that can be used with this ability.\n\n| D20    | Effect |\n|:-------:|:-------:|\n| 1        | ???    |\n| 2 - 5   | extra Grimm Slots are still expended,  stunned until the start of the next turn |\n| 6 - 19 | extra Grimm Slots are still expended |\n| 20      | the extra Grimm Slots are not expended |\n___\n\nThe Soul Chimera last until a Long Rest or until the Grimm User chooses to drop the form or another Soul Chimera is Activated."
