     "action": "Bonus Action",
     "text": "As a bonus action, the Grimm User can expend a Grimm Slot to invoke the power of Víðarr, gaining a number of Ash Curses equal to their Proficiency Bonus. The Grimm User chooses a damage type (except all-mighty damage) and applies the Ash Curses to one or more creatures they can see. Each Ash Curse has the following effects:\n\t\n* **Attack and Spell Power Boost**: The Grimm User gains a +1 bonus to attack rolls, spell attack rolls, and spell save DC for each Ash Curse applied to a creature.\n\t\n* **Bonus Damage:** Attacks against cursed creatures deal an additional 1d8 of the chosen damage type for each Ash Curse applied.\n\t\n* **Explosion Effect:** As an action, the Grimm User can detonate all active Ash Curses, dealing 1d10 of the chosen damage type per Ash Stack. A creature gains 1 Ash Stack at the end of each of its turns for every Ash Curse applied. If the curses remain for 1 minute, they automatically explode as a free action at the start of the Grimm User's turn. \n\t\n* **Critical Pain**: When the Grimm User deals a critical hit to a creature with active ash stacks, it can choose to explode the Ash Curse and add that damage to the attack damage.\n\t\n* **Ash Stack:** While curses are active, the Grimm User can use a bonus action to increase the Ash Stacks on each affected creature by 1.\n___\nAsh Curses persist until the creature dies, 1 minutes goes by or the Grimm User willingly removes them. If the Grimm User uses this ability again while Ash Curses are still active, all active curses immediately disappear."
