     "action": "Action",
     "text": "As a **Action**, the Grimm User expends **Two Grimm Slots** and gains the power of Makoa into its lungs and releases a aiding breath weapon. The Grimm User emits a number of waves equivalent to its **Proficiency Bonus**. For each wave the Grimm User can select one of the following effects:\n\n* **Healing Wave**: The Grimm User emits a wave of healing energy towards allies in a cone of **20 x Prof. Bonus ft.** which heals for number of **d8s x The Grimm User Prof. Bonus**. If a ally reaches its maximum health and some healing remains the leftover is converted to Temporary Hit Points. This wave does not affect summoned creatures nor transformations as its only ment to target the living and real bodies.\n\n* **Inspiring Wave**: The Grim User emits an wave of energy that inspires allies. All allies in a radius of **20 x Prof. Bonus ft** receive a number of **d8s** equivalent to the **Grimm User's Prof. Bonus / 2** (rounded down) and a Bonus to AC until the end of the Grimm User's Next turn equivalent to its Prof Bonus. Within the next 10 minutes, the ally can roll the die and add the number rolled to one ability check, attack roll, or saving throw it makes. The ally can wait until after it rolls the d20 before deciding to use the Inspiration die, but must decide before the DM says whether the roll succeeds or fails. Once the Inspiration die is rolled, it is lost.\n\n* **Wrecking Wave**: The Grimm Users emits a powerful breath attacks that could shatter the hardest crystal. A stroke of energy forming a line **30 x Prof. Bonus ft.** long and 5 feet wide blasts out from the Grimm Users in a direction of its choosing. Each creature in the line must make a Dexterity saving throw against a DC equal to the Grimm User spell casting DC. A creature takes a number of **d8 equivalent to the Grimm User's Total Level** of all mighty damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. This wave deals double the damage to Structures and Constructs.\n\n___\nIf there is more than one type of wave used in the Breath Of Life. Add the additional effect to the sum of it instead of resolving one by one."
